  "body": "**Blocked by:** #135\n\n## Context\n\nA project agent may advance its own time-based work, but event heartbeats have no meaningful execution without an item.\n\n## Task\n\nRegister `heartbeat.trigger({heartbeatId})`, scoped from the current persisted run exactly like list/history. For `dailyTime`, `weekly`, `interval`, and `everyNDays`, enqueue the existing heartbeat execution payload `{heartbeatId,triggeredByRunId}`; the handler writes `triggered_by='heartbeat'`, `heartbeat_id`, and `parent_run_id=triggeredByRunId`. Use manual key `heartbeat-fire:manual:${heartbeatId}` distinct from scheduler key `heartbeat-fire:${heartbeatId}`. An event rule returns 409 `heartbeat_event_triggered` and enqueues nothing. Do not require capability or approval beyond the tool's project-scoped availability. Manual execution must not modify schedule timestamps; audit fix #84 later adds scheduled occurrences while preserving this discriminator branch.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Tool, rule validation, payload attribution, distinct dedup key, and canonical error.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Run-now UI, event trigger without item, approval, and scheduled-occurrence generation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Manual and pending scheduled work cannot overwrite attribution.\n- Repeated pending manual triggers collapse to one job.\n- Event rule returns the exact 409 without side effects.\n- Child run history identifies the invoking parent.\n",
